</figure>
<figure id="S4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11983v1/images/LlamA/combined_perplexity_comparison.png" id="S4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/303;" width="429" height="303" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Comparison of validation perplexity and computational time for all competing methods in training LLaMA models.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We apply low-rank Muon, Muon, AdamW, and SGD with momentum (SGDM) for pretraining LLaMA. Similar to Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 GPT-2 pretraining ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we implement two versions of low-rank Muon with rank parameters <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use AdamW to train the embedding and head layers for Muon and low-rank Muon. We initialize all methods with the same weights from pretrained LLaMA models, and terminate all methods after one training epoch, consisting of 5000 iterations. We compare all methods using validation perplexity. The algorithmic parameters are carefully tuned to suit each method well in terms of computational performance. More details about the experimental setups including algorithm and LLaMA model parameters are deferred to Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Experimental details ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We visualize the top 100 singular values of the momentum updates <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with the Q, K, and V matrices for a 350M LLaMA model trained by Muon on the FineWeb100B dataset in Figure <a href="#S4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 4.3 LLaMA pretraining ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. The first and second rows of the figure display the top 100 singular values across different training iterations and neural network layers, respectively. This visualization partly supports the low-rank nature of the momentum updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We present a comparison of the validation perplexity and computational time in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3 LLaMA pretraining ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. From this table, we observe that our low-rank Muon consistently achieves better validation perplexity compared to Muon for the majority of model sizes and tested datasets, while vastly improving upon the validation perplexity achieved by AdamW and SGDM. We also
observe that the computational time of our low-rank Muon improves upon that of vanilla Muon, though all Muon-type methods remain slower than SGDM and AdamW. These observations demonstrate that our low-rank orthogonalization produces more generalizable LLaMA models across all tested model sizes and datasets. Moreover, it reduces computational time compared to the Newton-Schulz iterations for orthogonalization, although the improvement is less significant than the gains discussed in Sections 3.1 and 4.1. This is because most of the computational time is dominated by the forward and backward passes of the neural networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We plot the convergence behavior of validation perplexity versus training iterations in Figure <a href="#S4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 4.3 LLaMA pretraining ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. From this figure, we observe that for the model size of 60M, we observe that all Muon-type methods significantly outperforms AdamW and SGDM, while our low-rank Muon has similar performance compared to the vanilla Muon. For the 135M and 350M model size, we observe that our low-rank Muon significantly outperforms the vanilla Muon and other training methods. These observations support that our low-rank Muon consistently outperforms all other methods for training LLaMA models.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the above observations, we conclude that our low-rank Muon improves upon existing methods for training LLaMA models across the model sizes and datasets we tested.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Proof of the main results</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proofs of our main results presented in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, specifically Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first provide three technical lemmas, whose proofs can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Lemmas 1 to 3]</cite> and are therefore omitted here. The next lemma provides an expansion for the <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-power of the Frobenius norm, generalizing the well-known identity <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U+V\|_{F}^{2}=\|U\|_{F}^{2}+2\langle U,V\rangle+\|V\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U+V\|_{F}^{2}=\|U\|_{F}^{2}+2\langle U,V\rangle+\|V\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and inequality <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U+V\|_{F}^{2}\leq(1+c)\|U\|_{F}^{2}+(1+1/c)\|V\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U+V\|_{F}^{2}\leq(1+c)\|U\|_{F}^{2}+(1+1/c)\|V\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|U+V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha}+\alpha\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha-2}\langle U,V\rangle+2\|V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|U+V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha}+\alpha\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha-2}\langle U,V\rangle+2\|V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|U+V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq(1+c)\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha}+(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})\|V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},c&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|U+V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq(1+c)\|U\|_{F}^{\alpha}+(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})\|V\|_{F}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},c&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma provides an estimation of the partial sums of series.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> be a convex univariate function. Then we have <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{r=a}^{b}\zeta(r)\leq\int^{b+1/2}_{a-1/2}\zeta(\tau)\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{r=a}^{b}\zeta(r)\leq\int^{b+1/2}_{a-1/2}\zeta(\tau)\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for any integers <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a-1/2,b+1/2]\subset\mathrm{dom}\,\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>dom</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a-1/2,b+1/2]\subset\mathrm{dom}\,\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, one has</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.EGx25.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.EGx25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{r=a}^{b}\frac{1}{r^{\beta}}\leq\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\ln\big(b+\frac{1}{2}\big)-\ln\big(a-\frac{1}{2}\big)&amp;\text{if }\beta=1,\\[4.0pt]
\frac{1}{1-\beta}\big(\big(b+\frac{1}{2}\big)^{1-\beta}-\big(a-\frac{1}{2}\big)^{1-\beta}\big)&amp;\text{if }\beta\in(0,1)\cup(1,+\infty).\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{r=a}^{b}\frac{1}{r^{\beta}}\leq\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\ln\big(b+\frac{1}{2}\big)-\ln\big(a-\frac{1}{2}\big)&amp;\text{if }\beta=1,\\[4.0pt]
\frac{1}{1-\beta}\big(\big(b+\frac{1}{2}\big)^{1-\beta}-\big(a-\frac{1}{2}\big)^{1-\beta}\big)&amp;\text{if }\beta\in(0,1)\cup(1,+\infty).\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We next give a lemma that will be used to derive complexity bounds for our methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in(0,e^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in(0,e^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> be given. Then, it holds that <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{-\beta}\ln v\leq 2u\beta^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{-\beta}\ln v\leq 2u\beta^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\geq(u^{-1}\ln(u^{-1}))^{1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\geq(u^{-1}\ln(u^{-1}))^{1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We next establish a descent property for <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> along a matrix-signed direction.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,M\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,M\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be given, and let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{+}=X-\eta\mathrm{msgn}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>msgn</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{+}=X-\eta\mathrm{msgn}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(X^{+})\leq f(X)-\eta\|\nabla f(X)\|_{*}+2\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(X^{+})\leq f(X)-\eta\|\nabla f(X)\|_{*}+2\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of the matrix-sign function, one has <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle=\|M\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle=\|M\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then follows from these and (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) with <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=X^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=X^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(X^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(X^{+})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{f-descent}}{\leq}f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),X^{+}-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|X^{+}-X\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{f-descent}}{\leq}f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),X^{+}-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|X^{+}-X\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(X)+\langle M,X^{+}-X\rangle+\langle\nabla f(X)-M,X^{+}-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|X^{+}-X\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(X)+\langle M,X^{+}-X\rangle+\langle\nabla f(X)-M,X^{+}-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|X^{+}-X\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X)-\eta\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle+\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X)-\eta\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle+\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(X)-\eta\|M\|_{*}+\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(X)-\eta\|M\|_{*}+\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X)-\eta\|\nabla f(X)\|_{*}+2\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X)-\eta\|\nabla f(X)\|_{*}+2\eta\|\nabla f(X)-M\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta^{2}}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality is due to <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{+}=X-\eta\mathrm{msgn}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>msgn</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{+}=X-\eta\mathrm{msgn}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> and the trace Hölder inequality, the second equality is due to <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|_{*}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{msgn}(M)\|_{*}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle=\|M\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle M,\mathrm{msgn}(M)\rangle=\|M\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last inequality follows from the triangular inequality. Hence, the conclusion (<a href="#S5.E22" title="In Lemma 4. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) holds as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Proof of the main results in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="S5.SS1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, Theorem 10.5]</cite>. Next, we prove (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Low-rank orthogonalization ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). Let <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{T}M=U_{Q}\Sigma V^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{T}M=U_{Q}\Sigma V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the reduced SVD of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{T}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{T}M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> have orthogonal columns, and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal. Denote <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=QU_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=QU_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> have orthogonal columns, we obtain that <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> also has orthogonal columns; thus, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QQ^{T}M=U\Sigma V^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QQ^{T}M=U\Sigma V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a reduced SVD of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QQ^{T}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QQ^{T}M</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{msgn}(QQ^{T}M)=UV^{T}=QU_{Q}V^{T}=Q\mathrm{msgn}(Q^{T}M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>msgn</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{msgn}(QQ^{T}M)=UV^{T}=QU_{Q}V^{T}=Q\mathrm{msgn}(Q^{T}M)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Proof of the main results in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we provide proofs of Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="S5.SS2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall from Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{k}_{O}=\mathrm{msgn}(M_{Q}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{k}_{O}=\mathrm{msgn}(M_{Q}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,X^{+},M,\eta)=(X^{k},X^{k+1},M_{Q}^{k},\eta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,X^{+},M,\eta)=(X^{k},X^{k+1},M_{Q}^{k},\eta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(X^{k+1})\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(X^{k+1})\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Summing (<a href="#S5.E23" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.2 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) over <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\ldots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\ldots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X^{K})\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X^{K})\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\mathrm{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\mathrm{low}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X^{K})\overset{\eqref{ineq:f-descent-muond-1}}{\leq}f(X^{0})-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E23" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.2 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X^{K})\overset{\eqref{ineq:f-descent-muond-1}}{\leq}f(X^{0})-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X^{0})-\eta_{K-1}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X^{0})-\eta_{K-1}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality is due to the fact that <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing. Rearranging this inequality and using (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{ineq:flow-fx0-error-f}}{\leq}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}}{K\eta_{K-1}}+\frac{1}{K\eta_{K-1}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E24" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.2 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{ineq:flow-fx0-error-f}}{\leq}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}}{K\eta_{K-1}}+\frac{1}{K\eta_{K-1}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{def:eta-delta-d-f}}{=}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{1}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(\frac{2\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}}{(k+1)^{1/2}}+\frac{L_{*}}{2(k+1)}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{def:eta-delta-d-f}}{=}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{1}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(\frac{2\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}}{(k+1)^{1/2}}+\frac{L_{*}}{2(k+1)}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*}\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}}{(k+1)^{1/2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*}\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}}{(k+1)^{1/2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq\ln(2K+1)\leq 2\ln K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq\ln(2K+1)\leq 2\ln K</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> due to (<a href="#S5.EGx25" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Hence, the conclusion (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) holds as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="S5.SS2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 4 ‣ Algorithm 3 ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), and the same arguments as for proving (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{0\leq k\leq K-1}\{\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{0\leq k\leq K-1}\{\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{ineq:conv-gurara-1}\eqref{upbd-apx-error}}{\leq}\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*})\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{\delta_{k}}{(k+1)^{1/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E8" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E9" title="In 4 ‣ Algorithm 3 ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{ineq:conv-gurara-1}\eqref{upbd-apx-error}}{\leq}\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*})\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{\delta_{k}}{(k+1)^{1/2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{def:eta-delta-d}}{=}\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*})\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E11" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{def:eta-delta-d}}{=}\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*})\ln K}{K^{1/2}}+\frac{2}{K^{1/2}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*}+4)\ln K}{K^{1/2}}\overset{\eqref{def:Ud}}{=}\frac{U_{\mathrm{gd}}\ln K}{K^{1/2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E10" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>gd</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+L_{*}+4)\ln K}{K^{1/2}}\overset{\eqref{def:Ud}}{=}\frac{U_{\mathrm{gd}}\ln K}{K^{1/2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq\ln(2K+1)\leq 2\ln K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq\ln(2K+1)\leq 2\ln K</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> due to (<a href="#S5.EGx25" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). In addition, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,u,v)=(1/2,\epsilon/(4U_{\mathrm{gd}}),K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>gd</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,u,v)=(1/2,\epsilon/(4U_{\mathrm{gd}}),K)</annotation></semantics></math>, one can see that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle K^{-1/2}\ln K\leq\frac{\epsilon}{U_{\mathrm{gd}}}\qquad\forall K\geq\Big(\frac{4U_{\mathrm{gd}}}{\epsilon}\ln\Big(\frac{4U_{\mathrm{gd}}}{\epsilon}\Big)\Big)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ln</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>gd</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>gd</mi></msub></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>gd</mi></msub></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K^{-1/2}\ln K\leq\frac{\epsilon}{U_{\mathrm{gd}}}\qquad\forall K\geq\Big(\frac{4U_{\mathrm{gd}}}{\epsilon}\ln\Big(\frac{4U_{\mathrm{gd}}}{\epsilon}\Big)\Big)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which along with (<a href="#S5.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.2 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) implies that Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.2 Low-rank matrix-signed gradient descent ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Proof of the main results in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we begin by establishing some technical lemmas and use them to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. For convenience, we define a sequence of potentials for Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> as follows:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{P}_{k}:=f(X^{k})+p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|^{\alpha}_{F}\qquad\forall k\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{P}_{k}:=f(X^{k})+p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|^{\alpha}_{F}\qquad\forall k\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the sequence <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of positive scalars that will be specified separately later. The following lemma presents a recurrence relation for the estimation error of the gradient estimators <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> hold. Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> be generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with input parameters <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq(1-\theta_{k})\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall k\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq(1-\theta_{k})\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}\qquad\forall k\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In 4 ‣ Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\overset{\eqref{update-mk}}{=}(1-\theta_{k})M^{k}+\theta_{k}G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E12" title="In 4 ‣ Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\overset{\eqref{update-mk}}{=}(1-\theta_{k})M^{k}+\theta_{k}G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))+\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))+\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice from (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 6 ‣ Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{O}^{k}=\mathrm{msgn}(M_{Q}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{O}^{k}=\mathrm{msgn}(M_{Q}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which along with (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 7 ‣ Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) implies that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X^{k+1}-X^{k}\|=\eta_{k}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M^{k}_{Q})\|\leq\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X^{k+1}-X^{k}\|=\eta_{k}\|\mathrm{msgn}(M^{k}_{Q})\|\leq\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, it follows from Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}\leq\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}\leq\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using these, (<a href="#S5.E18" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E19" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), and (<a href="#S5.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{rela-mk+1-pm}}{=}\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))+\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{rela-mk+1-pm}}{=}\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))+\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{open-alpha}}{\leq}\|(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}+2\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E18" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{open-alpha}}{\leq}\|(1-\theta_{k})(M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k}))+(1-\theta_{k})(\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}+2\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|\theta_{k}(G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1}))\|_{F}^{\alpha}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{open-alpha-2}}{\leq}(1+c)(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E19" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{open-alpha-2}}{\leq}(1+c)(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+c)(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+L_{*}^{\alpha}(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+c)(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+L_{*}^{\alpha}(2+(\alpha-1)^{\alpha-1}c^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality is due to (<a href="#S5.E18" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the second inequality is due to (<a href="#S5.E19" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|G(X^{k+1};\xi^{k+1})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last inequality is due to <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}\leq L_{*}\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(X^{k})-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}\leq L_{*}\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Lemma 5. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) clearly holds. For <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, letting <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(1-\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(1-\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha}-1</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), and using the fact that <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c^{1-\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c^{1-\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=((1-\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha}-1)^{1-\alpha}=\Big(\frac{1}{(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha-1}}-1\Big)^{1-\alpha}\leq\Big(\frac{1}{1-(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}-1\Big)^{1-\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=((1-\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha}-1)^{1-\alpha}=\Big(\frac{1}{(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha-1}}-1\Big)^{1-\alpha}\leq\Big(\frac{1}{1-(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}-1\Big)^{1-\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\frac{1-(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}{(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}\Big)^{\alpha-1}\leq((\alpha-1)\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\frac{1-(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}{(\alpha-1)\theta_{k}}\Big)^{\alpha-1}\leq((\alpha-1)\theta_{k})^{1-\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\tau)^{\beta}\leq 1-\beta\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\tau)^{\beta}\leq 1-\beta\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this inequality with (<a href="#S5.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), one has</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq(1-\theta_{k})\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+L_{*}^{\alpha}(2+\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\|M^{k+1}-\nabla f(X^{k+1})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq(1-\theta_{k})\|M^{k}-\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{F}^{\alpha}+L_{*}^{\alpha}(2+\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha})(1-\theta_{k})^{\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which along with <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math> implies that (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Lemma 5. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) holds as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma establishes a descent property for the potential sequence <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{P}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{P}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> defined below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> hold. Let <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> be generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with input parameters <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},\delta_{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},\delta_{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2 Notation and assumptions ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> be given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varrho:=\min\{m,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϱ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varrho:=\min\{m,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{P}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{P}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined in (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) for <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> and any nonincreasing positive sequence <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\mathcal{P}_{k+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\mathcal{P}_{k+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{P}_{k}-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{P}_{k}-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\qquad\forall k\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\qquad\forall k\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> that <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{O}^{k}=\mathrm{msgn}(M^{k}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{O}^{k}=\mathrm{msgn}(M^{k}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M^{k}-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}\leq\delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M^{k}-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}\leq\delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using these and (<a href="#S5.E22" title="In Lemma 4. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) with <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{+},X,M,\eta)=(X^{k+1},X^{k},M_{Q}^{k},\eta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{+},X,M,\eta)=(X^{k+1},X^{k},M_{Q}^{k},\eta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(X^{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(X^{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M_{Q}^{k}\|_{*}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
