<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U\|_{*}\leq\varrho^{1/2}\|U\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U\|_{*}\leq\varrho^{1/2}\|U\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fact that <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing. In addition, letting <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}=\alpha/(\alpha-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}=\alpha/(\alpha-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and using the Young’s inequality, we obtain that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\eta_{k}\varrho^{1/2}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\eta_{k}\varrho^{1/2}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\big((\alpha\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/\alpha}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}\big)^{\alpha}}{\alpha}+\frac{(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k}/(\alpha\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/\alpha})^{\alpha^{\prime}}}{\alpha^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\big((\alpha\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/\alpha}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}\big)^{\alpha}}{\alpha}+\frac{(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k}/(\alpha\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/\alpha})^{\alpha^{\prime}}}{\alpha^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta_{k}p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}^{\alpha}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta_{k}p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}^{\alpha}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">This along with (<a href="#S5.E32" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) implies that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\mathcal{P}_{k+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\xi^{k+1}}[\mathcal{P}_{k+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})+p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}^{\alpha}-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(X^{k})+p_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})-M^{k}\|_{F}^{\alpha}-\eta_{k}\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">The conclusion (<a href="#S5.E30" title="In Lemma 6. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) then follows from this and (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="S5.SS3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> be generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},\delta_{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},\delta_{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> given in (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), and
<math id="S5.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\mathcal{P}}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\mathcal{P}}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined in (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) with such <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X^{k},M^{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the following <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{k}=(k+1)^{(\alpha^{2}-3\alpha+2)/(3\alpha-2)}\qquad\forall k\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{k}=(k+1)^{(\alpha^{2}-3\alpha+2)/(3\alpha-2)}\qquad\forall k\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, one can see that <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing. Also, observe from (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) that <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{k}\}\subset(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{k}\}\subset(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{k}\}\subset(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{k}\}\subset(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},p_{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\eta_{k},\theta_{k},p_{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the assumptions in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. In addition, by (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E33" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), one has that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{0}]=f(X^{0})+p_{0}\mathbb{E}[\|M^{0}-\nabla f(X^{0})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]=f(X^{0})+\mathbb{E}[\|G(X^{0};\xi^{0})-\nabla f(X^{0})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq f(X^{0})+\sigma^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{0}]=f(X^{0})+p_{0}\mathbb{E}[\|M^{0}-\nabla f(X^{0})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]=f(X^{0})+\mathbb{E}[\|G(X^{0};\xi^{0})-\nabla f(X^{0})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\leq f(X^{0})+\sigma^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{K}]=\mathbb{E}[f(X^{K})+p_{K}\|M^{K}-\nabla f(X^{K})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\geq\mathbb{E}[f(X^{K})]\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{K}]=\mathbb{E}[f(X^{K})+p_{K}\|M^{K}-\nabla f(X^{K})\|_{F}^{\alpha}]\geq\mathbb{E}[f(X^{K})]\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation on both sides of (<a href="#S5.E30" title="In Lemma 6. ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) with respect to <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi^{i}\}_{i=0}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi^{i}\}_{i=0}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{k+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{P}_{k}]-\eta_{k}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{P}_{k}]-\eta_{k}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\qquad\forall k\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\qquad\forall k\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Summing up this inequality over <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\ldots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\ldots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and using (<a href="#S5.E34" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E35" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\mathrm{low}}\overset{\eqref{lwbd-exq-Pk-pm}}{\leq}\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{K}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E35" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\mathrm{low}}\overset{\eqref{lwbd-exq-Pk-pm}}{\leq}\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{K}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{0}]-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[{\mathcal{P}}_{0}]-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{upbd-exq-P0-pm}}{\leq}f(X^{0})+\sigma^{\alpha}-\eta_{K-1}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E34" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{upbd-exq-P0-pm}}{\leq}f(X^{0})+\sigma^{\alpha}-\eta_{K-1}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}\eta_{k})^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{\alpha^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from (<a href="#S5.E34" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) and the fact that <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing. Rearranging the terms in
(<a href="#S5.E36" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), and using (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), and (<a href="#S5.E33" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), we obtain that for all <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]\overset{\eqref{rear-pot-desc-pm}}{\leq}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}}{K\eta_{K-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E36" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]\overset{\eqref{rear-pot-desc-pm}}{\leq}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}}{K\eta_{K-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{1}{K\eta_{K-1}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}\eta_{k}^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{1}{K\eta_{K-1}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(2\eta_{k}\delta_{k}+\frac{L_{*}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}+\frac{(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}\eta_{k}^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}}{(\theta_{k}p_{k})^{1/(\alpha-1)}}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{1-\alpha}\eta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}+2\sigma^{\alpha}\theta_{k}^{\alpha}p_{k}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{pm-eta-theta}\eqref{def:pk-pm}}{=}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E16" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S5.E33" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\eqref{pm-eta-theta}\eqref{def:pk-pm}}{=}\frac{f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{1}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(\frac{L_{*}}{2(k+1)^{2(2\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}+\frac{2+(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}}{k+1}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{1}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\Big(\frac{L_{*}}{2(k+1)^{2(2\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}+\frac{2+(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}+3L_{*}^{\alpha}+2\sigma^{\alpha}}{k+1}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}+2L_{*}+4+2(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}+6L_{*}^{\alpha}+4\sigma^{\alpha})\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\overset{\eqref{def:Umn}}{=}\frac{U_{\mathrm{mn}}\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#S3.E15" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{(f(X^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+\sigma^{\alpha}+2L_{*}+4+2(\alpha-1)(2\varrho^{1/2}/\alpha)^{\alpha/(\alpha-1)}+6L_{*}^{\alpha}+4\sigma^{\alpha})\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\overset{\eqref{def:Umn}}{=}\frac{U_{\mathrm{mn}}\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq 2\ln K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)\leq 2\ln K</annotation></semantics></math> due to (<a href="#S5.EGx25" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)^{2(2\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}\leq(3\alpha-2)2^{\alpha/(3\alpha-2)}/\alpha&lt;4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}1/(k+1)^{2(2\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}\leq(3\alpha-2)2^{\alpha/(3\alpha-2)}/\alpha&lt;4</annotation></semantics></math> due to (<a href="#S5.EGx25" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3\alpha-2)/\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3\alpha-2)/\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly selected from <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,\ldots,K-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,\ldots,K-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then follows from this and the above inequality that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{\iota_{K}})\|_{*}]=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]\leq\frac{U_{\mathrm{mn}}\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\qquad\forall K\geq 3." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{\iota_{K}})\|_{*}]=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(X^{k})\|_{*}]\leq\frac{U_{\mathrm{mn}}\ln K}{K^{(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}}\qquad\forall K\geq 3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with <math id="S5.SS3.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,u,v)=((\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2),(\alpha-1)\epsilon/(2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}),K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,u,v)=((\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2),(\alpha-1)\epsilon/(2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}),K)</annotation></semantics></math>, one can see that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle K^{-(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}\ln K\leq\frac{\epsilon}{U_{\mathrm{mn}}}\qquad\forall K\geq\Big(\frac{2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}}{(\alpha-1)\epsilon}\ln\Big(\frac{2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}}{(\alpha-1)\epsilon}\Big)\Big)^{(3\alpha-2)/(\alpha-1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>ln</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>mn</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K^{-(\alpha-1)/(3\alpha-2)}\ln K\leq\frac{\epsilon}{U_{\mathrm{mn}}}\qquad\forall K\geq\Big(\frac{2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}}{(\alpha-1)\epsilon}\ln\Big(\frac{2(3\alpha-2)U_{\mathrm{mn}}}{(\alpha-1)\epsilon}\Big)\Big)^{(3\alpha-2)/(\alpha-1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">which together with (<a href="#S5.E37" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 5.3 Proof of the main results in Section ‣ 5 Proof of the main results ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) implies that Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Low-rank Muon ‣ 3 Matrix optimization with low-rank orthogonalization ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> holds.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Concluding remarks</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we introduce a new low-rank orthogonalization approach as a lightweight substitute for the popular orthogonalization approach by Newton-Schulz iterations. Based on this low-rank orthogonalization, we propose low-rank Muon and illustrate its advantages over existing training methods through experiments on GPT-2 and LLaMA pretraining. Theoretically, we also establish complexity bounds for the proposed low-rank Muon under heavy-tailed noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A key ingredient of our low-rank orthogonalization is the construction of a column-orthogonal matrix <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, inspired by low-rank matrix approximation techniques. A valuable future research direction is to explore alternative strategies for constructing <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Some such alternatives are presented in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Low-rank orthogonalization procedures ‣ Low-rank orthogonalization for large-scale matrix optimization with applications to foundation model training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
